0064;16;14;By this time, The Force Awakens was widely marketed and promoted ahead of its premier, finally releasing on December 18, 2015. According to industry reports, The Force Awakens had an estimated budget of $200 million USD, ultimately earning $2.069 billion USD by the end of its original theatrical run in early 2016, making it the highest grossing Star Wars film. Soon after, principal photography began on Episode VIII in February. The second season of Star Wars Rebels ended on March 30, 2016, with the episode "Twilight of the Apprentice." Celebration Europe was held in London from July 15 to July 17. On July 22, Episode VIII finished principal photography. Keeping with the format, the first two episodes of Rebels Season Three released as a film titled Star Wars Rebels: Steps Into Shadow, which released on September 24, 2016. The episodes began airing weekly on October 1. Rogue One: A Star Wars Story released in the United Kingdom on December 15, with the standard release the following day on the 16th of December. On January 23, 2017, the title for Episode VIII of the Star Wars saga was revealed to be The Last Jedi. On March 3, the fourth season of Star Wars Rebels was confirmed, with the third season of ending on March 25 with the two part episode special "Zero Hour." Celebration Orlando, the largest Star Wars Celebration Event with 70,000 participants took place from April 13 to April 16.
0064;17;597499;The Solo: A Star Wars Story soundtrack is the score for the film Solo: A Star Wars Story, composed by John Powell. It was released on May 25, 2018, the same day as the film itself. A Deluxe Edition was released on November 20, 2020, featuring a longer soundtrack. Along with the soundtrack for Star Wars: Episode VIII The Last Jedi, the soundtrack was nominated for Grammy awards in the categories of Best Instrumental Composition and Score Soundtrack For Visual Media.
